 359  *==============================================================================
 360  *  Periods
 361  *==============================================================================
 362  * The set TIME is the period of time for which we have projections for GDP,
 363  * population and economically active population .
 364  TIME Time periods
 365  /
 366  2019*2050
 367  *2019*2038
 368  *2019*2025
 369  *2019
 370  /
 371  T(time)
 372  T1(time)         First period;
 373  T1(time)         = yes$[ord(time) eq 1];
 374   
 375  *===============================================================================
 376   
 377  ALIAS (j,jj)
 378  ALIAS (i,ii,ij)
 379  ALIAS (l,lj)
 380  ALIAS (k,kj)
 381  ALIAS (z,zj,zjj)
 382  ALIAS (power, power2)
 383  AlIAS (ENE,ENE2)
 384  ;
 385   
 386  * If you don't want the model to run to the horizon defined in the set
 387  * TIME, define parameter EndTime as the final year for model resolution.
 388  *Parameter EndTime /2008/;
 389  *Parameter EndTime /2020/;
 390  Parameter EndTime /2050/;
 391   
 392  *$EXIT
