 503  *==============================================================================
 504  *  2.2 Variables - Benchmark
 505  *==============================================================================
 506  *  Benchmark values of variables are parameters. Their acronyms are the
 507  *  corresponding variable names,followed by the letter "O".
 508   
 509  *==============================================================================
 510  *   2.2.1 Volume variables
 511  *==============================================================================
 512   CABXO(z)        Current account balance of region z in terms of the international currency (pseudo-volume variable)
 513   CO(i,z)         Consumption of commodity i by households in region z
 514   CGO(i,z)        Public consumption of commodity i in region z
 515   CIO(j,z)        Total intermediate consumption of industry j in region z
 516   CEO(j,z)        Total energy intermediate consumption of industry j in region z
 517   CMINO(i,z)      Minimum consumption of commodity i by households in region z
 518   CTH_REALO(z)    Real household consumption in region z
 519   DDO(i,z)        Domestic demand for commodity i produced locally in region z
 520   DIO(i,j,z)      Intermediate consumption of commodity i by industry j in region z
 521   DEO(ene,j,z)    Intermediate energy consumption of commodity i by industry j in region z
 522   DITO(i,z)       Total intermediate demand of commodity i in region z
 523   DSO(j,i,z)      Supply of commodity i by sector j to the domestic market
 524   DSO_I(i,z)      Supply of commodity i to the domestic market of region z
 525   DSO_J(j,z)      Supply of activity j to the domestic market of region z
 526   EXO(i,z,zj)     Quantity of product i exported by country z to country zj
 527   EXTO(i,z)       Supply of composite commodity i by region z to the export market
 528   EXTTO(j,i,z)    Supply of activity j to the export market i of region z
 529   G_REALO(z)      Current real government expenditures on goods and services in region z
 530   GDP_BP_REALO(z) Real GDP at basic prices
 531   GDP_MP_REALO(z) Real GDP at market prices
 532   GDP_BP_W_REALO  Real GDP at basic prices
 533   IMO(i,zj,z)     Quantity of product i imported by country z from country zj
 534   IMTO(i,z)       Quantity demanded of composite imports of commodity i by region z
 535   INDO(k,j,z)     Volume of new type k capital investment to industry j in region z
 536   INVO(i,z)       Final demand of commodity i for investment purposes (GFCF) in region z
 537   IT_REALO(z)     Real gross fixed capital formation
 538   KDO(k,j,z)      Demand for type k capital by industry j in region z
 539   KDCO(j,z)       Demand for composite capital by industry j in region z
 540   KSO(k,z)        Supply of type k capital in region z
 541   KSTO(z)         Total supply of capital in region z
 542   LDO(l,j,z)      Demand for type l labor by industry j in region z
 543   LDCO(j,z)       Demand for composite labor by industry j in region z
 544   LSO(l,z)        Supply of type l labor in region z
 545   MRGNO(i,z)      Domestic production of commodity i in region z exported as international margin services
 546   POPO(z)         Population in 2019
 547   QO(i,z)         Quantity demanded of composite commodity i in region z
 548   VAO(j,z)        Value added of industry j in region z
 549   KLEO(j,z)       KLE of industry j in region z
 550   XSO_I(i,z)      Commoidty i total production
 551   XSO(j,i,z)      Total output of industry j in region z
 552   XSTO(j,z)       Total output of industry j
 553   POWERQO(z)      Total power output in region z
 554   
 555  *==============================================================================
 556  *   2.2.2 Price variables
 557  *==============================================================================
 558   eO(z)           Exchange rate (price of international currency in terms of region z local currency)
 559   IRO(z)          Interest rate
 560   PO(i,z)         Basic price of commodity i in region z
 561   PO2(j,i,z)      Basic price of industry js production of commodity i
 562   PO3(i,j,z)
 563   PO4(i,j,z)
 564   PPOWERO(z)
 565   PIO(i,z)
 566   PTO(j,z)        Basic price of industry js output
 567   PCO(i,z)        Purchaser price of composite commodity i (including all taxes and margins) in region z
 568   PCIO(j,z)       Intermediate consumption price index of industry j in region z
 569   PCEO(j,z)       Intermediate energy consumption price index of industry j in region z
 570   PDO(i,z)        Price of local product i sold on region z domestic market (including all taxes)
 571   PEO(i,z,zj)     Price received for commodity i exported to region zj by region z (excluding export taxes)
 572   PETO(i,z)       Border price of composite commodity i exported by region z
 573   PIXCONO(z)      Consumer price index in region z
 574   PIXGDPO(z)      GDP deflator in region z
 575   PIXGDP_WO       World GDP deflator
 576   PIXGVTO(z)      Public expenditures price index in region z
 577   PIXINVO(z)      Investment price index in region z
 578   PKO(z)          Price of new capital in region z
 579   PLO(i,z)        Price of local product i (excluding all taxes on products) in region z
 580   PMO(i,zj,z)     Price of commodity i imported by region z from region zj (including all taxes duties and margins)
 581   PMTO(i,z)       Price of composite commodity i imported by region z (including all taxes duties and margins)
 582   PPO(j,z)        Unit cost of industry j in region z including taxes directly related to the use of capital and labor but excluding other taxes on production
 583   PVAO(j,Z)       Price of industry j value added in region z (including taxes on production directly related to the use of capital and labor)
 584   PKLEO(j,z)      Price of industry j KLE in region z
 585   PWMO(i,zj,z)    World price of commodity i imported from country zj by region z (expressed in international currency)
 586   PWMGO(i)        World price of margin i (expressed in international currency)
 587   PWXO(i,z,zj)    World price of commodity i exported to country zj by region z (expressed in international currency)
 588   RO(k,j,z)       Rental rate of type k capital in industry j of region z
 589   RCO(j,z)        Rental rate of industry j composite capital in region z
 590   RKO(k,z)        Rental rate of type k capital in region z
 591   RTIO(k,j,z)     Rental rate paid by industry j for type k capital in region z including capital taxes
 592   UO(z)           User cost of capital in region z
 593   WO(l,z)         Wage rate of type l labor in region z
 594   WCO(j,z)        Wage rate of industry j composite labor in region z
 595   WTIO(l,j,z)     Wage rate paid z by industry j for type l labor in region including payroll taxes
 596   
 597  *==============================================================================
 598  *   2.2.3 Nominal (value) variables
 599  *==============================================================================
 600   CABO(z)         Current account balance of region z
 601   CTHO(z)         Consumption budget of households in region z
 602   DEPO(z)         Amount of depreciation (capital consumption allowance) in region z
 603   GO(z)           Current government expenditures on goods and services in region z
 604   GDP_BPO(z)      Region z GDP at basic prices
 605   GDP_BP_WO       World GDP at basic prices
 606   GDP_FDO(z)      Region z GDP at purchasers prices from the perspective of final demand
 607   GDP_IBO(z)      Region z GDP at market prices (income-based)
 608   GDP_MPO(z)      Region z GDP at market prices
 609   ITO(z)          Total investment expenditures in region z
 610   RKDO(k,j,z)     Type k capital income in industry j in region z
 611   SGO(z)          Government savings in region z
 612   SHO(z)          Household savings in region z
 613   SROWO(z)        Rest-of-the-world savings with respect to region z
 614   TDHO(z)         Household income taxes in region z
 615   TICO(i,z)       Government revenue from indirect taxes on commodity i in region z
 616   TICTO(z)        Total government receipts of indirect taxes on commodities in region z
 617   TIKO(k,j,z)     Government revenue from taxes on type k capital used by industry j in region z
 618   TIKTO(z)        Total government revenue from from taxes on capital in region z
 619   TIMO(i,zj,z)    Government revenue from duties on commodity i imported from region zj by region z
 620   TIMTO(z)        Total government revenue from import duties in region z
 621   TIPO(j,z)       Government revenue from taxes on industry j production in region z (excluding taxes directly related to the use of capital and labor)
 622   TIPTO(z)        Total government revenue from production taxes in region z (excluding taxes directly related to the use of capital and labor)
 623   TIWO(l,j,z)     Government revenue from payroll taxes on type l labor in industry j of region z
 624   TIWTO(z)        Total government revenue from payroll taxes in region z
 625   TIXO(i,z,zj)    Government revenue from export taxes on commodity i exported by region z to region zj
 626   TIXTO(z)        Total government revenue from export taxes in region z
 627   TPRCTSO(z)      Total government revenue from taxes on products and imports in region z
 628   TPRODNO(z)      Total government revenue from other taxes on production in region z
 629   YDHO(z)         Household disposable income in region z
 630   YGO(z)          Total government income in region z
 631   YHO(z)          Household total income in region z
 632   YHKO(z)         Household capital income in region z
 633   YHLO(z)         Household labor income in region z
 634   YROWO(z)        Rest-of-the-world total income from region z
 635   
 636  *==============================================================================
 637  *   2.2.4 Rates and intercepts
 638  *==============================================================================
 639   phiO(z)         Scale variable (allocation of investment to industries)
 640   sh0O(z)         Intercept (household savings)
 641   sh1O(z)         Slope (household savings)
 642   ttdh0O(z)       Intercept (household income tax)
 643   ttdh1O(z)       Slope (household income tax)
 644   tticO(i,z)      Tax rate on commodity i
 645   ttikO(k,j,z)    Tax rate on capital k used in industry j
 646   ttimO(i,zj,z)   Rate of taxes and duties on imports of commodity i from country zj
 647   ttipO(j,z)      Tax rate on the production of industry j
 648   ttiwO(l,j,z)    Tax rate on type l worker compensation in industry j
 649   ttixO(i,z,zj)   Export tax rate on exported commodity x
 650  ;
 651   
 652  Scalar
 653   Tiny small figure / 0.000000000001/ ;
 654   
 655  *==============================================================================
 656  * 3 Data
 657  *==============================================================================
 658  *  3.1 Data input from GTAP8.1
 659  *==============================================================================
 660  *   3.1.1 Reading data aggregated with DATA_AGG-2007.gms
 661  *==============================================================================
 662  *  The PEP w-t model uses aggregated data from GTAP8.1. The following file
 663  *  includes data for some variables and substitution elasticities.
 664   
--- LOAD  CO = 13:CO
--- LOAD  CGO = 14:CGO
--- LOAD  DDO = 15:DDO
--- LOAD  DEPO = 16:DEPO
--- LOAD  DIO = 17:DIO
--- LOAD  DSO = 18:DSO
--- LOAD  DSO_I = 19:DSO_I
--- LOAD  EXO = 20:EXO
--- LOAD  IMO = 21:IMO
--- LOAD  INVO = 22:INVO
--- LOAD  KSTO = 23:KSTO
--- LOAD  LDO = 24:LDO
--- LOAD  MRGNO = 25:MRGNO
--- LOAD  XSO = 39:XSO
--- LOAD  XSO_I = 40:XSO_I
--- LOAD  XSTO = 41:XSTO
--- LOAD  TOT_POP = 61:TOT_POP
--- LOAD  g_GDP = 62:g_GDP
--- LOAD  g_POP = 63:g_POP
--- LOAD  g_SDR = 64:g_SDR
--- LOAD  AEEI_low = 65:AEEI_low
--- LOAD  AEEI_high = 66:AEEI_high
--- LOAD  TREND = 67:TREND
--- LOAD  CTAX_Cal = 68:CTAX_Cal
--- LOAD  CTAX_CPS = 69:CTAX_CPS
--- LOAD  CTAX_NZS = 70:CTAX_NZS
--- LOAD  CTAX_61 = 71:CTAX_61
--- LOAD  CTAX_145 = 72:CTAX_145
--- LOAD  CTAX_285 = 73:CTAX_285
--- LOAD  CTAX_425 = 74:CTAX_425
--- LOAD  CTAX_565 = 75:CTAX_565
--- LOAD  RKDO = 27:RKDO
--- LOAD  TDHO = 28:TDHO
--- LOAD  TICO = 30:TICO
--- LOAD  TIKO = 31:TIKO
--- LOAD  TIMO = 32:TIMO
--- LOAD  TIPO = 33:TIPO
--- LOAD  TIWO = 34:TIWO
--- LOAD  TIXO = 35:TIXO
--- LOAD  tmrg = 38:tmrg
--- LOAD  sigma_M1 = 43:sigma_M1
--- LOAD  sigma_M2 = 44:sigma_M2
--- LOAD  sigma_VA = 45:sigma_VA
--- LOAD  sigma_KLE = 46:sigma_KLE
--- LOAD  POPO = 26:POPO
 668   
 669  display sigma_M1, sigma_M2 ;
 670   
 671  sigma_M1('04_GAS',Z) = 6;
 672   
 673  sigma_M2('03_OIL',Z) = 2;
 674  sigma_M2('04_GAS',Z) = 2;
 675   
 676  sigma_M1('03_OIL','06_PRK') = 0.5;
 677   
 678  *sigma_M1('10_PETROLCOAL','05_mng') = 6;
 679   
 680  *sigma_M2('19_CONSTRUC',Z) = 0.5;
 681   
 682  display sigma_M1, sigma_M2 ;
 683   
 684  *==============================================================================
 685  *   3.1.2 Rescaling the variables
 686  *==============================================================================
 687  * GTAP 8.1 data are in millions of (2004 and 2007) US dollars
 688  * (see www.gtap.agecon.purdue.edu/resources/download/5679.pdf)
 689  * With RES = 10000, model results are in tens of billions (10G$)
 690  RES              = 10000;
 691  *RES              = 1;
 692   
 693   
 694  * NOTE: In GTAP parlance, "agents' prices" are prices paid by buyers, and
 695  *       "market prices" are prices received by sellers.
 696   
 697  * Household consumption = GTAP domestic purchases (VDPA) + import purchases (VIPA)
 698  * by households at agents' prices.
 699  CO(i,z)          = CO(i,z)/RES;
 700   
 701  * Public final consumption = domestic purchases (VDGA) + import purchases (VIGA)
 702  * by government at agents' prices.
 703  CGO(i,z)         = CGO(i,z)/RES;
 704   
 705  * Domestic purchases = domestic absorption:
 706  * (CO + CGO + INVO + DIO) - [ imports (IMO) + transport margins (tmrg)
 707  *                              + indirect taxes (TICO + TIMO) ]
 708  DDO(i,z)         = DDO(i,z)/RES;
 709   
 710  * Capital depreciation (DEP)
 711  DEPO(z)          = DEPO(z)/RES;
 712   
 713  * Intermediate consumption = domestic purchases (VDFA) + import purchases (VIFA)
 714  * by firms belonging to sectors other than CGDS, at agents' prices.
 715  DIO(i,j,z)       = DIO(i,j,z)/RES;
 716   
 717  * Domestic supply = domestic demand (DDO) in GTAP_AGG.gms
 718  DSO(j,i,z)        = DSO(j,i,z)/RES;
 719  DSO_I(i,z)        = DSO_I(i,z)/RES;
 720   
 721  * Exports = exports at world prices (VXWD) = imports at world prices
 722  * Note: the GTAP variable VXWD is NOT used in the DATA_AGG.gms program; the
 723  * value recorded in DATA_AGG.gdx is actually identical to IMO
 724  EXO(i,z,zj)      = EXO(i,z,zj)/RES;
 725   
 726  * Imports = imports at world prices (VIWS) - sum of transport margins on imports (VTWR)
 727  IMO(i,z,zj)      = IMO(i,z,zj)/RES;
 728   
 729  * Demand for investment purposes = domestic purchases (VDFA)+ import purchases (VIFA)
 730  * by firms of the CGDS sector at agents' prices.
 731  INVO(i,z)        = INVO(i,z)/RES;
 732   
 733  * Total capital stock at the beginning of the period (VKB)
 734  KSTO(z)          = KSTO(z)/RES;
 735   
 736  * Labor demand = Remuneration of labor at market prices, before taxes
 737  * (components of VFM, "primary factor purchases, by households, at market prices")
 738  LDO(l,j,z)       = LDO(l,j,z)/RES;
 739   
 740  * Supply of transport margins at market prices (VST), adjusted proportionately
 741  * so that MRGNO = sum of tmrg for every margin commodity
 742  MRGNO(i,z)       = MRGNO(i,z)/RES;
 743   
 744  * Remuneration of capital at market prices, before taxes
 745  * (components of VFM, "primary factor purchases, by households, at market prices")
 746  RKDO(k,j,z)      = RKDO(k,j,z)/RES;
 747   
 748  * Direct taxes = factor payment at market prices (VFM)
 749  *                - primary factor sales at agents' prices (EVOA)
 750  TDHO(z)          = TDHO(z)/RES;
 751   
 752  * Domestic taxes on commodities = demand at agents' prices - demand at market prices:
 753  * Include 6 pairs of GTAP components
 754  *       VDPA - VDPM
 755  *       VIPA - VIPM
 756  *       VDGA - VDGM
 757  *       VIGA - VIGM
 758  *       VDFA - VDFM
 759  *       VIFA - VIFM
 760  TICO(i,z)        = TICO(i,z)/RES;
 761   
 762  * Net taxes on factor of production = factor employment tax revenue (FTRV)
 763  *                                     - factor-based subsidies (FBEP).
 764  TIKO(k,j,z)      = TIKO(k,j,z)/RES;
 765   
 766  * Import duties = "ordinary" import duties (TFRV)
 767  TIMO(i,z,zj)     = TIMO(i,z,zj)/RES;
 768   
 769  * Taxes on production = MINUS "ordinary output subsidies" (OSEP)
 770  TIPO(j,z)        = TIPO(j,z)/RES;
 771   
 772  * Net taxes on factor of production = factor employment tax revenue (FTRV)
 773  *                                     - factor-based subsidies (FBEP).
 774  TIWO(l,j,z)      = TIWO(l,j,z)/RES;
 775   
 776  * Taxes on exports = export tax equivalent of the Multi-Fiber Agreement (MFA)
 777  * quota premium(MFRV) + "ordinary" export taxes (XTRV)
 778  TIXO(i,z,zj)     = TIXO(i,z,zj)/RES;
 779   
 780  * Transport margins at world prices = sum of margins on imports (VTWR)
 781  tmrg(i,ij,z,zj)  = tmrg(i,ij,z,zj)/RES;
 782   
 783  * Domestic output = domestic supply (DSO) + supply of transport margins (MRGNO)
 784  *                   + exports (EXO) - taxes on exports (TIXO)
 785   
 786  XSO_I(i,z)        = XSO_I(i,z)/RES;
 787  XSO(j,i,z)        = XSO(j,i,z)/RES;
 788  XSTO(j,z)         = XSTO(j,z)/RES;
 789   
 790  growthz(z)        = 0.02;
 791   
 792  *==============================================================================
 793  *  3.3 Exogenous prices and parameters
 794  *==============================================================================
 795   
 796  *  Price elasticity (should be equal to one to verify homogeneity)
 797  eta = 1;
 798   
 799  *==============================================================================
 800  * CES and CET elasticities
 801  *==============================================================================
 802  * CES elasticities are defined using GTAP8.1 data for imports
 803  * (sigma_M1 and sigma_M2) and value added (sigma_VA)
 804   
 805  * Other exogenous parameters can be defined if the Excel file VAL_PAR.XLS
 806  PARAMETER
 807  PARZ;
 808   
GDXIN   C:\Users\kimc0\GUIDE_GLOBAL_CGE\2.RD_CGE\Input_w-t\PAR.gdx
--- LOAD  sigma_KD = 1:sigma_KD
--- LOAD  sigma_LD = 2:sigma_LD
--- LOAD  sigma_X1 = 4:sigma_X1
--- LOAD  sigma_X2 = 5:sigma_X2
--- LOAD  sigma_X3 = 6:sigma_X3
--- LOAD  sigma_X0 = 7:sigma_X0
--- LOAD  sigma_Y = 8:sigma_y
--- LOAD  sigma_INV = 10:sigma_inv
--- LOAD  PARZ = 9:PARZ
 812   
 813  sigma_INV(k,j,z) = 2;
 814  *$exit
 815   
 816  *sigma_VA('03_OIL','06_PRK') = 2;
 817   
 818  sigma_Y('03_OIL','06_PRK') = 1.01;
 819   
 820   
 821  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 822  * CES - composite capital
 823  * We assume that the elasticity between the different type of capital
 824  * is twice that used for value added.
 825  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 826  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls and delete following line:
 827   sigma_KD(j,z)   = 2*sigma_VA(j,z);
 828  * sigma_KD(j,z)   = 0.5;
 829   
 830  * sigma_KD('27_CONSTRUC', '05_MNG') = 0.2;
 831  *27_CONSTRUC 05_MNG  2.52
 832   
 833  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 834  * CES - composite labor
 835  * We assume that the elasticity between the different type of labor
 836  * is twice that used for value added.
 837  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 838  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls and delete following line:
 839   sigma_LD(j,z)   = 2*sigma_VA(j,z);
 840  * sigma_LD(j,z)   = 0.5;
 841   
 842  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 843  * CES - composite KLE, ENER
 844   sigma_KLE(j,z)  = 0.5 ;
 845   sigma_ENER(j,z) = 1.1 ;
 846   
 847  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 848  * CET - total output
 849  * We arbitrarily assume that the transformation elasticity between total exports,
 850  * domestic supply and margins is equal to 2 for all sectors and all region.
 851  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 852  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls.
 853   
 854  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 855  * CET - exports
 856  * We arbitrarily assume that the transformation elasticity between exports
 857  * to the different partners is equal to 3 for all sectors and all region.
 858  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 859  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls.
 860   
 861  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 862  * LES parameters - Frisch
 863  * We assume that the Frisch parameter is -1.1 for rich regions/countries and
 864  * -1.5 for other regions/countries.
 865   frisch(zrich)   = -1.1;
 866   frisch(zother)  = -1.5;
 867   
 868  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 869  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls, delete the previous 2 lines and uncomment the
 870  * following line:
 871   frisch(z)      = PARZ(z,'frisch');
 872   
 873  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 874  * LES parameters - Income elasticity of consumption
 875  * We arbitrarily assume that the income elasticity of the consumption of
 876  * commodity i is the same for all region/country.
 877  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 878  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls.
 879   
 880  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 881  *  Slopes of taxation functions
 882  *   One can either choose to assign a value to the intercepts and calibrate
 883  *   the slopes accordingly, or the other way around. This type of modelling
 884  *   can be useful to take into account known marginal savings or taxation rates
 885  *   or to deal with negative average saving rates in cases where savings are
 886  *   negative for some household groups.
 887  *   When no further information is available, one can simply set the intercepts
 888  *   to zero and calibrate an average rate: this is what we do here for ttdh0O.
 889  *   If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 890  *   the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls.
 891  * ttdh0O(z)       = PARZ(z,'ttdh0O');
 892   
 893   ttdh0O(z)       = 0;
 894  *   The slope ttdh1O is calibrated below in the mane GAMS file
 895   
 896  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 897  *  Elasticity - Investment demand function
 898  * We arbitrarily assume that this elasticity is equal to 2 for all types of
 899  * capital, all sectors and all regions.
 900  * If the user wishes to assume otherwise, he can fill the appropriate area in
 901  * the Excel file VAL_PAR.xls.
 902   
 903  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 904  * Also we need to assign values to some prices
 905  * All of the prices below, EXCEPT eO, may be set at arbitrary values
 906  * without loss of generality.
 907  *
 908  * In the case of eO, although exchange rates may be given arbitrary values
 909  * in the model, they must all be equal for calibration at this stage. The reason
 910  * is that the supply of margin transport services MRGNO must equal global demand.
 911  * Since there is a single world price for international transport margins
 912  * (rather than bilateral world prices for other commodities) the unit of
 913  * measurement of the volume of margin services must be the same for all regions,
 914  * and in turn, that implies that the divisor that converts the nominal value to
 915  * volume be the same for all regions. Since that divisor involves the exchange
 916  * rate, all exchange rates must be equal.
 917   
 918  * Normally, prices that may be given arbitrary values are set at 1:
 919   eO(z)           = 1;
 920   PEO(i,z,zj)     = 1;
 921   PLO(i,z)        = 1;
 922   PWMGO(i)        = 1;
 923   WO(l,z)         = 1;
 924   
 925  *==============================================================================
 926  * 4 Calibration
 927  *==============================================================================
 928  *  4.1 Calculation of income and savings related variables and parameters
 929  *==============================================================================
 930   YHKO(z)         = SUM[(k,j),RKDO(k,j,z)];
 931   YHLO(z)         = SUM[(l,j),LDO(l,j,z)];
 932   YHO(z)          = YHLO(z)+YHKO(z);
 933   YDHO(z)         = YHO(z)-TDHO(z);
 934   CTHO(z)         = SUM[i,CO(i,z)];
 935   SHO(z)          = YDHO(z)-CTHO(z);
 936   
 937   TICTO(z)        = SUM[i,TICO(i,z)];
 938   TIMTO(z)        = SUM[(i,zj),TIMO(i,zj,z)];
 939   TIWTO(z)        = SUM[(l,j),TIWO(l,j,z)];
 940   TIKTO(z)        = SUM[(k,j),TIKO(k,j,z)];
 941   TIPTO(z)        = SUM[j,TIPO(j,z)];
 942   TIXTO(z)        = SUM[(i,zj),TIXO(i,z,zj)];
 943   TPRODNO(z)      = TIKTO(z)+TIWTO(z)+TIPTO(z);
 944   TPRCTSO(z)      = TICTO(z)+TIMTO(z)+TIXTO(z);
 945   YGO(z)          = TDHO(z)+TPRCTSO(z)+TPRODNO(z);
 946   GO(z)           = SUM[i,CGO(i,z)];
 947   SGO(z)          = YGO(z)-GO(z);
 948   
 949   YROWO(z)        = SUM[(i,zj),IMO(i,zj,z)]+SUM[(i,ij,zj),tmrg(i,ij,zj,z)];
 950   SROWO(z)        = YROWO(z)-SUM[(i,zj),EXO(i,z,zj)]-SUM[i,MRGNO(i,z)];
 951   CABO(z)         = -SROWO(z);
 952   
 953   ITO(z)          = SHO(z)+SGO(z)+SROWO(z);
 954   
 955  *==============================================================================
 956  *  4.2 Calibration of parameters and other variables
 957  *==============================================================================
 958  *  4.2.1 Calibration of investment and government spending shares
 959  *==============================================================================
 960   gamma_GVT(i,z)  = CGO(i,z)/SUM[ij,CGO(ij,z)];
 961   gamma_INV(i,z)  = INVO(i,z)/SUM[ij,INVO(ij,z)] ;
 962   
 963  *==============================================================================
 964  *  4.2.2 Calibration of other prices and revised volumes (part 1)
 965  *==============================================================================
 966   LDO(l,j,z)      = LDO(l,j,z)/WO(l,z);
 967   LDCO(j,z)       = SUM[l,LDO(l,j,z)];
 968   LSO(l,z)        = SUM[j,LDO(l,j,z)];
 969   EXO(i,z,zj)     = [EXO(i,z,zj)-TIXO(i,z,zj)]/PEO(i,z,zj);
 970   EXTO(i,z)       = SUM[zj,EXO(i,z,zj)];
 971   
 972   PWXO(i,z,zj)$EXO(i,z,zj)
 973                   = {[PEO(i,z,zj)*EXO(i,z,zj)+TIXO(i,z,zj)]/EXO(i,z,zj)}/eO(z);
 974   
 975   PETO(i,z)       = SUM[zj,PEO(i,z,zj)*EXO(i,z,zj)]/EXTO(i,z);
 976   PWMO(i,z,zj)    = PWXO(i,z,zj);
 977   IMO(i,zj,z)     = EXO(i,zj,z);
 978   IMTO(i,z)       = SUM[zj,IMO(i,zj,z)];
 979   
 980   DSO(j,i,z)       = DSO(j,i,z)/PLO(i,z);
 981   DSO_I(i,z)       = SUM(j,DSO(j,i,z));
 982   DSO_J(j,z)       = SUM(i,DSO(j,i,z));
 983   QO(i,z)         = IMTO(i,z)+DDO(i,z);
 984   
 985   MRGNO(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)
 986                   = MRGNO(i,z)/[eO(z)*PWMGO(i)];
 987   
 988   XSO_I(i,z)      = EXTO(i,z)+DDO(i,z)+MRGNO(i,z);
 989   
 990   XSTO(j,z)       = sum(i, XSO(j,i,z));
 991   
 992   PO(i,z)        = [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)+PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)
 993                    +eO(z)*PWMGO(i)*MRGNO(i,z)]/XSO_I(i,z);
 994   
 995   PO2(j,i,z)$XSO(j,i,z) = 1;
 996   
 997   PO3(i,j,z)$XSO(j,i,z) = 1;
 998   
 999   PIO(i,z)       = SUM[j$XSO(j,i,z),PO2(J,I,z)*XSO(j,i,z)]/XSO_I(i,z);
1000   
1001   PTO(j,z)       = SUM[i$XSO(j,i,z),PO2(j,i,z)*XSO(j,i,z)]/XSTO(j,z);
1002   
1003   PPO(j,z)       = [SUM[l,TIWO(l,j,z)+WO(l,z)*LDO(l,j,z)]
1004                    +SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)+RKDO(k,j,z)]
1005                    +SUM[nene,DIO(nene,j,z)]+SUM[ene,DIO(ene,j,z)]]/XSTO(j,z);
1006   
1007   theta2(j,i,z) = DSO(j,i,z)/sum(jj, DSO(jj,i,z));
1008   
1009   EXTTO(j,i,z)$DSO(j,i,z) = theta2(j,i,z)*EXTO(i,z);
1010   
1011  *==============================================================================
1012  *  4.3 Calibration of tax rates, margins, prices and volumes
1013  *==============================================================================
1014  *  4.3.1 Margin rates and tax rates
1015  *==============================================================================
1016   ttixO(i,z,zj)   = [eO(z)*PWXO(i,z,zj)/PEO(i,z,zj)]-1;
1017   tticO(i,z)      = TICO(i,z)/{PLO(i,z)*DDO(i,z)
1018                     +SUM[zj,IMO(i,zj,z)*eO(z)*PWMO(i,zj,z)
1019                     +TIMO(i,zj,z)+SUM[ij,tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)]]};
1020   
1021   tmrg(i,ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
1022                   = tmrg(i,ij,zj,z)/(PWMGO(i)*eO(z)*IMO(ij,zj,z));
1023   
1024   ttimO(i,zj,z)$IMO(i,zj,z)
1025                   = TIMO(i,zj,z)/{IMO(i,zj,z)*eO(z)*(PWMO(i,zj,z)
1026                    +SUM[ij,PWMGO(ij)*tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)])};
1027   
1028   ttiwO(l,j,z)$LDO(l,j,z)
1029                   = TIWO(l,j,z)/[WO(l,z)*LDO(l,j,z)];
1030   
1031   ttikO(k,j,z)$RKDO(k,j,z)
1032                   = TIKO(k,j,z)/RKDO(k,j,z);
1033   
1034   ttipO(j,z)      = [PTO(j,z)/PPO(j,z)]-1;
1035   
1036   ttdh1O(z)       = [TDHO(z)-ttdh0O(z)]/YHO(z);
1037   
1038  *==============================================================================
1039  *  4.3.2 Calibration of other prices and revised volumes (part 2)
1040  *==============================================================================
1041   PDO(i,z)        = PLO(i,z)*(1+tticO(i,z));
1042   PMO(i,zj,z)     = eO(z)*(PWMO(i,zj,z)+SUM[ij,PWMGO(ij)*tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)])
1043                   *(1+ttimO(i,zj,z))*(1+tticO(i,z));
1044   PMTO(i,z)       = SUM[zj,PMO(i,zj,z)*IMO(i,zj,z)]/IMTO(i,z);
1045   PCO(i,z)        = [PMTO(i,z)*IMTO(i,z)+PDO(i,z)*DDO(i,z)]/QO(i,z);
1046   
1047   CO(i,z)         = CO(i,z)/PCO(i,z);
1048   CGO(i,z)        = CGO(i,z)/PCO(i,z);
1049   DIO(nene,j,z)   = DIO(nene,j,z)/PCO(nene,z);
1050   DEO(ene,j,z)    = DIO(ene,j,z)/PCO(ene,z);
1051   INVO(i,z)       = INVO(i,z)/PCO(i,z);
1052   
1053   CIO(j,z)        = SUM[nene,DIO(nene,j,z)];
1054   CEO(j,z)        = SUM[ene,DEO(ene,j,z)];
1055   
1056   DITO(nene,z)     = SUM[j,DIO(nene,j,z)];
1057   DITO(ene,z)      = SUM[j,DEO(ene,j,z)];
1058   
1059   PO4(ene,j,z)    = PCO(ene,z);
1060   
1061   PCIO(j,z)       = SUM[nene,PCO(nene,z)*DIO(nene,j,z)]/CIO(j,z);
1062   PCEO(j,z)       = SUM[ene,PCO(ene,z)*DEO(ene,j,z)]/CEO(j,z) ;
1063   
1064   WTIO(l,j,z)     = WO(l,z)*(1+ttiwO(l,j,z));
1065   
1066   WCO(j,z)$LDCO(j,z)
1067                   = SUM[l,WTIO(l,j,z)*LDO(l,j,z)]/LDCO(j,z);
1068   
1069  *==============================================================================
1070  *  4.4 Calibration of dynamic parameters
1071  *==============================================================================
1072  * Calibration of dynamic parameters following new procedure.
1073  * The price of capital is arbitrary:
1074   PKO(z) = 1;
1075   
1076  * The calibration of depreciation rates is based on two hypotheses:
1077  * 1. The rate of depreciation is the same for all types of capital and all
1078  *    industries in each region (this hypothesis is made to accommodate the fact
1079  *    that, in the GTAP data base, capital consumption allowance is not detailed;
1080  *    as a matter of fact, the GTAP capital consumption allowance is set at
1081  *    4% of the value of the capital stock).
1082  * 2. The rental rate of capital is uniform across industries and types of
1083  *    capital in each region.
1084  * 3. The investment rate (IND/KD) is uniform across industries and types of
1085  *    capital in each region.
1086  * These hypotheses lead to the following formulae:
1087   
1088  * From GTAP, we know KSTO.
1089   KSTO(z)         = KSTO(z)/PKO(z);
1090   
1091  * Assuming a uniform depreciation rate for all types
1092  * of capital and all industries:
1093   delta(z)        = DEPO(z)/[PKO(z)*KSTO(z)];
1094   
1095  * From GTAP, we know KSTO. Assuming a uniform rental rate R for all types
1096  * of capital and all industries:
1097   RO(k,j,z)$RKDO(k,j,z)
1098                   = SUM[(kj,jj),RKDO(kj,jj,z)]/KSTO(z);
1099   
1100  * Then from the GTAP value of income paid to capital RKD we calibrate KDO:
1101   KDO(k,j,z)$RKDO(k,j,z)
1102                   = RKDO(k,j,z)/RO(k,j,z);
1103   
1104  * The supply of capital is equal to demand:
1105   KSO(k,z)        = SUM[j,KDO(k,j,z)];
1106   
1107  * The rate of return on capital, net of depreciation, is:
1108   IRO(z)         = {SUM[(k,j)$RKDO(k,j,z),RKDO(k,j,z)]-DEPO(z)}/[PKO(z)*KSTO(z)];
1109   
1110  * The user cost of capital follows
1111   UO(z)           = PKO(z)*(IRO(z)+delta(z));
1112   
1113  * Combining
1114  * - the hypothesis of uniform investment rates
1115  * - the hypothesis of uniform rental rates
1116  * - the hypothesis of uniform depreciation rates
1117  * leads to
1118   phiO(z)         = [ITO(z)/PKO(z)]/KSTO(z);
1119   
1120  * Investment by destination follows:
1121   INDO(k,j,z)$KDO(k,j,z)
1122                   = phiO(z)*KDO(k,j,z);
1123   
1124   A_K(z)          = 1/PKO(z)*{PROD[i$gamma_INV(i,z),(PCO(i,Z)/gamma_INV(i,z))
1125                     **gamma_INV(i,z)]};
1126   
1127   KDCO(j,z)       = SUM[k,KDO(k,j,z)];
1128   RTIO(k,j,z)     = RO(k,j,z)*(1+ttikO(k,j,z));
1129   RCO(j,z)$KDCO(j,z)
1130                   = SUM[k,RTIO(k,j,z)*KDO(k,j,z)]/KDCO(j,z);
1131   
1132  *==============================================================================
1133  *  4.5 Calibration of other prices and revised volumes (part 3)
1134  *==============================================================================
1135   VAO(j,z)        = LDCO(j,z)+KDCO(j,z);
1136   
1137   PVAO(j,z)       = [WCO(j,z)*LDCO(j,z)+RCO(j,z)*KDCO(j,z)]/VAO(j,z);
1138   
1139  * PIXGDPO is tautologically equal to 1, based on its formula
1140  * PIXGDPO(z)      = {SUM[j,{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)]
1141  *                   /SUM[j,{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)]
1142  *                   *SUM[j,{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)]
1143  *                   /SUM[j,{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)]}**0.5;
1144   PIXGDPO(z)      = 1;
1145   
1146  * PIXGDP_WO is tautologically equal to 1, based on its formula
1147  * PIXGDP_WO       = {SUM[(j,z),{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)/eO(z)]
1148  *                   /SUM[(j,z),{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)/eO(z)]
1149  *                   *SUM[(j,z),{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)/eO(z)]
1150  *                   /SUM[(j,z),{(PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)+TIPO(j,z))/VAO(j,z)}*VAO(j,z)]/eO(z)}**0.5;
1151   PIXGDP_WO       = 1;
1152   
1153  * PIXCONO(z) is tautologically equal to 1, based on its formula
1154  * PIXCONO(z)      = SUM[i,PCO(i,z)*CO(i,z)]
1155  *                  /SUM[i,PCO(i,z)*CO(i,z)];
1156   PIXCONO(z)      = 1;
1157   
1158  * PIXINVO(z) is tautologically equal to 1, based on its formula
1159  * PIXINVO(z)      = PROD[i$gamma_INV(i,z),(PCO(i,z)/PCO(i,z))**gamma_INV(i,z)];
1160   PIXINVO(z)      = 1;
1161   
1162  * PIXGVTO(z) is tautologically equal to 1, based on its formula
1163  * PIXGVTO(z)      = PROD[i$gamma_GVT(i,z),(PCO(i,z)/PCO(i,z))**gamma_GVT(i,z)];
1164   PIXGVTO(z)      = 1;
1165   
1166  *==============================================================================
1167  *  4.6 Calibration of function parameters
1168  *==============================================================================
1169  *   4.6.1 Leontief functions
1170  *==============================================================================
1171   io(j,z)         = CIO(j,z)/XSTO(j,z) ;
1172   
1173   io2(j,z)        = CEO(j,z)/XSTO(j,z) ;
1174   
1175   v(j,z)          = VAO(j,z)/XSTO(j,z) ;
1176   
1177   v2(j,z)         = (CEO(j,z)+VAO(j,z))/XSTO(j,z) ;
1178   
1179   aij(nene,j,z)   = DIO(nene,j,z)/CIO(j,z);
1180   aij2(ene,j,z)   = DEO(ene,j,z)/CEO(j,z);
1181   
1182   aij2_t(ene,j,z,time) =  aij2(ene,j,z)*AEEI_low(z,'2019') ;
1183   io2_t(j,z,time) = io2(j,z)*AEEI_low(z,'2019') ;
1184  *==============================================================================
1185  *   4.6.2 Calibration of CET parameters
1186  *==============================================================================
1187  *    4.6.2.1 CET between total exports, domestic supply and margins
1188  *==============================================================================
1189   rho_X1(i,z)     = (1+sigma_X1(i,z))/sigma_X1(i,z);
1190   
1191   beta_EX_X1(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)
1192                   = [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)$EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))]/
1193                     [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)$EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1194                     PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1195                     eO(z)*PWMGO(i)*MRGNO(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+Tiny];
1196   
1197   beta_EX_X1(i,z)$(MRGNO(i,z) eq 0)
1198                   = [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)$EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))]/
1199                     [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)$EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1200                     PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+Tiny];
1201   
1202   beta_D_X1(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)
1203                   = [PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))]/
1204                     [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1205                     PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1206                     eO(z)*PWMGO(i)*MRGNO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))];
1207   
1208   beta_D_X1(i,z)$(MRGNO(i,z) eq 0)
1209                   = [PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))]/
1210                     [PETO(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))+
1211                     PLO(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**(1-rho_X1(i,z))];
1212   
1213   B_X1(i,z)       = XSO_I(i,z)/[beta_EX_X1(i,z)*EXTO(i,z)**rho_X1(i,z)
1214                    +beta_D_X1(i,z)*DSO_I(i,z)**rho_X1(i,z)+(1-beta_EX_X1(i,z)
1215                    -beta_D_X1(i,z))*MRGNO(i,z)**rho_X1(i,z)]**(1/rho_X1(i,z));
1216   
1217  *==============================================================================
1218  *    4.6.2.2 CET between exports to different trading partners
1219  *==============================================================================
1220   rho_X2(i,z)     = (1+sigma_X2(i,z))/sigma_X2(i,z);
1221   beta_X2(i,z,zj)$EXO(i,z,zj)
1222                   = [PEO(i,z,zj)*EXO(i,z,zj)**(1-rho_X2(i,z))]/
1223                     SUM[zjj$EXO(i,z,zjj),PEO(i,z,zjj)*EXO(i,z,zjj)
1224                     **(1-rho_X2(i,z))];
1225   B_X2(i,z)       = EXTO(i,z)/{SUM[zj,beta_X2(i,z,zj)*EXO(i,z,zj)**rho_X2(i,z)]
1226                     **(1/rho_X2(i,z))};
1227   
1228  *==============================================================================
1229  *   4.6.3 Calibration of CES parameters
1230  *==============================================================================
1231  *    4.6.3.0 Composite output
1232  *==============================================================================
1233   rho_X3(i,z)   = (1-sigma_X3(i,z))/sigma_X3(i,z);
1234   
1235   beta_X3(j,i,z)$XSO(j,i,z)
1236                 = [PO2(j,i,z)*XSO(j,i,z)**(1+rho_X3(i,z))]/
1237                     SUM[jj$XSO(jj,i,z),PO2(jj,i,z)*XSO(jj,i,z)**(1+rho_X3(i,z))];
1238   
1239   B_X3(i,z)     = XSO_I(i,z)
1240                    /SUM[jj$XSO(jj,i,z),beta_X3(jj,i,z)*XSO(jj,i,z)**(-rho_X3(i,z))
1241                    ]**(-1/rho_X3(i,z));
1242   
1243   POWERQO(Z) = SUM(POWER, XSO(power,'18_ELEC',z));
1244   
1245  * sigma_X4(z) =2;
1246   sigma_X4(z) =2;
1247   
1248   rho_X4(z)   = (1-sigma_X4(z))/sigma_X4(z);
1249   
1250   beta_X4(power,z)
1251                 = [PO2(power,'18_ELEC',z)*XSO(power,'18_ELEC',z)**(1+rho_X4(z))]/
1252                     SUM[power2$XSO(power2,'18_ELEC',z),PO2(power2,'18_ELEC',z)*XSO(power2,'18_ELEC',z)**(1+rho_X4(z))];
1253   
1254   B_X4(z)     = POWERQO(Z)
1255                    /SUM[power2$XSO(power2,'18_ELEC',z),beta_X4(power2,z)*XSO(power2,'18_ELEC',z)**(-rho_X4(z))
1256                    ]**(-1/rho_X4(z));
1257   
1258   TnDShare(z) = XSO('18_TnD','18_ELEC',z) / XSO_I('18_ELEC',z);
1259   
1260   PPOWERO(z) = 1;
1261   
1262  *==============================================================================
1263  *    4.6.3.1 Composite good
1264  *==============================================================================
1265   rho_M1(i,z)     = (1-sigma_m1(i,z))/sigma_m1(i,z);
1266   beta_M1(i,z)    = PMTO(i,z)*IMTO(i,z)**(rho_M1(i,z)+1)/
1267                    {PDO(i,z)*DDO(i,z)**(rho_M1(i,z)+1)
1268                    +PMTO(i,z)*IMTO(i,z)**(rho_M1(i,z)+1)};
1269   B_M1(i,z)       = QO(i,z)/{beta_M1(i,z)*IMTO(i,z)**(-rho_M1(i,z))
1270                    +(1-beta_M1(i,z))*DDO(i,z)**(-rho_M1(i,z))}**(-1/rho_M1(i,z));
1271   
1272  *==============================================================================
1273  *    4.6.3.2 CES between imports from different trading partners
1274  *==============================================================================
1275   rho_M2(i,z)     = (1-sigma_M2(i,z))/sigma_M2(i,z);
1276   beta_M2(i,zj,z)$IMO(i,zj,z)
1277                   = [PMO(i,zj,z)*IMO(i,zj,z)**(rho_M2(i,z)+1)]/
1278                     SUM[zjj$IMO(i,zjj,z),PMO(i,zjj,z)*IMO(i,zjj,z)
1279                      **(rho_M2(i,z)+1)];
1280   B_M2(i,z)       = IMTO(i,z)/{SUM[zj$IMO(i,zj,z),beta_M2(i,zj,z)*IMO(i,zj,z)
1281                     **(-rho_M2(i,z))]**(-1/rho_M2(i,z))};
1282   
1283  *==============================================================================
1284  *    4.6.3.3 Composite capital
1285  *==============================================================================
1286   rho_KD(j,z)     = (1-sigma_KD(j,z))/sigma_KD(j,z);
1287   
1288   beta_KD(k,j,z)$KDO(k,j,z)
1289                   = [RTIO(k,j,z)*KDO(k,j,z)**(1+rho_KD(j,z))]/
1290                     SUM[kj$KDO(kj,j,z),RTIO(kj,j,z)*KDO(kj,j,z)**(1+rho_KD(j,z))];
1291   B_KD(j,z)$KDCO(j,z)
1292                   = KDCO(j,z)/{SUM[k$KDO(k,j,z),beta_KD(k,j,z)*KDO(k,j,z)
1293                     **(-rho_KD(j,z))]**(-1/rho_KD(j,z))};
1294   
1295  *==============================================================================
1296  *    4.6.3.4 Composite labor
1297  *==============================================================================
1298   rho_LD(j,z)     = (1-sigma_LD(j,z))/sigma_LD(j,z);
1299   beta_LD(l,j,z)$LDO(l,j,z)
1300                   = [WTIO(l,j,z)*LDO(l,j,z)**(1+rho_LD(j,z))]/
1301                     SUM[lj$LDO(lj,j,z),WTIO(lj,j,z)*LDO(lj,j,z)
1302                     **(1+rho_LD(j,z))];
1303   B_LD(j,z)$LDCO(j,z)
1304                   = LDCO(j,z)/{SUM[l$LDO(l,j,z),beta_LD(l,j,z)*LDO(l,j,z)
1305                     **(-rho_LD(j,z))]**(-1/rho_LD(j,z))};
1306   
1307  *===============================================================================
1308  *   Composite E
1309  *===============================================================================
1310   rho_ENER(j,z)   = (1-sigma_ENER(j,z))/sigma_ENER(j,z);
1311   
1312   beta_ENER(ene,j,z)$DEO(ene,j,z)
1313                   = [PO4(ene,j,z)*DEO(ene,j,z)**(1+rho_ENER(j,z))]/
1314                     SUM[ene2$DIO(ene,j,z),DEO(ene2,j,z)**(1+rho_ENER(j,z))];
1315   
1316   B_ENER(j,z)$CEO(j,z)
1317                   = CEO(j,z)/{SUM[ene$DEO(ene,j,z),beta_ENER(ene,j,z)*DEO(ene,j,z)
1318                     **(-rho_ENER(j,z))]**(-1/rho_ENER(j,z))};
1319   
1320   B_ENER_t(j,z,time) = B_ENER(j,z)*(1/AEEI_low(z,'2019'));
1321   
1322  *==============================================================================
1323  *    4.6.3.5 Value added
1324  *==============================================================================
1325   sigma_VA('10_PETROLCOAL',z) = 1.260;
1326   display sigma_VA ;
1327   
1328   rho_VA(j,z)     = (1-sigma_VA(j,z))/sigma_VA(j,z);
1329   
1330   beta_VA(j,z)$KDCO(j,z)
1331                   = WCO(j,z)*LDCO(j,z)**(rho_VA(j,z)+1)/
1332                    {WCO(j,z)*LDCO(j,z)**(rho_VA(j,z)+1)+
1333                     RCO(j,z)*KDCO(j,z)**(rho_VA(j,z)+1)};
1334   B_VA(j,z)$KDCO(j,z)
1335                   = VAO(j,z)
1336                     /{[beta_VA(j,z)*LDCO(j,z)**(-rho_VA(j,z))+
1337                     (1-beta_VA(j,z))*KDCO(j,z)**(-rho_VA(j,z))
1338                     ]**(-1/rho_VA(j,z))};
1339   
1340  *==============================================================================
1341  *    Composite KLE
1342  *==============================================================================
1343   KLEO(j,z)       = CEO(j,z) + VAO(j,z) ;
1344   
1345   PKLEO(j,z)      = [PCEO(j,z)*CEO(j,z)+PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)]/KLEO(j,z);
1346   
1347   rho_KLE(j,z)    = (1-sigma_KLE(j,z))/sigma_KLE(j,z);
1348   
1349   beta_KLE(j,z)$KLEO(j,z)
1350                   = PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)**(rho_KLE(j,z)+1)/
1351                    {PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)**(rho_KLE(j,z)+1)+
1352                     PCEO(j,z)*CEO(j,z)**(rho_KLE(j,z)+1)};
1353   
1354   beta_KLE2(j,z)$KLEO(j,z)
1355                   = 1-beta_KLE(j,z);
1356   
1357   B_KLE(j,z)$KLEO(j,z)
1358                   = KLEO(j,z)
1359                     /{[beta_KLE(j,z)*VAO(j,z)**(-rho_KLE(j,z))+
1360                     (beta_KLE2(j,z))*CEO(j,z)**(-rho_KLE(j,z))
1361                     ]**(-1/rho_KLE(j,z))};
1362   
1363   beta_KLE2_t(j,z,time) = beta_KLE2(j,z)*AEEI_low(z,'2019');
1364   
1365  *==============================================================================
1366  *   4.6.4 Calibration of LES parameters
1367  *==============================================================================
1368  *   As the assigned values of income elasticities may not result in
1369  *   consumption shares that add up to 1, this first step
1370  *   adjusts the elasticities proportionally
1371   sigma_Y(i,z)    = sigma_Y(i,z)/{SUM[ij,sigma_Y(ij,z)*PCO(ij,z)*CO(ij,z)]
1372                     /CTHO(z)};
1373   gamma_LES(i,z)  = PCO(i,z)*CO(i,z)*sigma_Y(i,z)/CTHO(z);
1374   CMINO(i,z)      = CO(i,z)+gamma_LES(i,z)*CTHO(z)/{PCO(i,z)*frisch(z)};
1375   
1376   elas_enecom(ene,z)  = CMINO(ene,z)/CO(ene,z)*(1-gamma_LES(ene,z)) -1 ;
1377   
1378  *==============================================================================
1379  *  4.7 Calibration of gross domestic products
1380  *==============================================================================
1381   GDP_BPO(z)      = SUM[j,PVAO(j,z)*VAO(j,z)]+TIPTO(z);
1382   GDP_MPO(z)      = GDP_BPO(z)+TPRCTSO(z);
1383   GDP_IBO(z)      = SUM[(l,j),WO(l,z)*LDO(l,j,z)]+SUM[(k,j),RO(k,j,z)*KDO(k,j,z)]
1384                     +TPRODNO(z)+TPRCTSO(z);
1385   GDP_FDO(z)      = SUM[i,PCO(i,z)*(CO(i,z)+CGO(i,z)+INVO(i,z))]
1386                    +eO(z)*SUM[(i,zj),PWXO(i,z,zj)*EXO(i,z,zj)]
1387                    +eO(z)*SUM[i,PWMGO(i)*MRGNO(i,z)]
1388                    -eO(z)*SUM[(i,zj),IMO(i,zj,z)*(PWMO(i,zj,z)
1389                    +SUM{ij,PWMGO(ij)*tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)})];
1390   GDP_BP_WO       = SUM[z,GDP_BPO(z)/eO(z)];
1391   
1392  *==============================================================================
1393  *  4.8 Calibration of real (volume) variables computed from price indices
1394  *==============================================================================
1395   CABXO(z)        = CABO(z)/[PIXGDP_WO*eO(z)];
1396   
1397  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1398  * Calculation of CAB index
1399  * If every region's CABX grows exogenously according to exogro, then the
1400  * worldwide sum of CABX's will not be zero. If, due to redundancy, the reference
1401  * region's CABX is left implicit, then it will not grow according to that
1402  * region's exogro (it follows that the solution will depend on the choice of
1403  * reference region). CABix is formed from exogro by inflating or deflating the
1404  * updating factors of positive (SURplus) and negative (DEFicit) CABX's in such
1405  * a way that their sum remains zero.
1406   
      Parameter CABXsur(z,time), CABXdef(z,time), bal(time), mu(time), CABix(z,time);
       CABXsur(z,time) = CABXO(z)*exogro(z,time)$[CABXO(z) gt 0];
       CABXdef(z,time) = CABXO(z)*exogro(z,time)$[CABXO(z) lt 0];
       Bal(time)       = sum(zj,CABXsur(zj,time))+sum(zj,CABXdef(zj,time));
       mu(time)        = sum(zj,CABXsur(zj,time))/
                           {sum(zj,CABXsur(zj,time))+sum(zj,abs[CABXdef(zj,time)])};
       CABXsur(z,time) = CABXsur(z,time)*{1-mu(time)*Bal(time)/sum(zj,CABXsur(zj,time))};
       CABXdef(z,time) = CABXdef(z,time)*{1-[1-mu(time)]*Bal(time)/sum(zj,CABXdef(zj,time))};
       CABix(z,time)   = [CABXsur(z,time)+CABXdef(z,time)]/CABXO(z);
1418  *------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1419   
1420   CTH_REALO(z)    = CTHO(z)/PIXCONO(z);
1421   G_REALO(z)      = GO(z)/PIXGVTO(z);
1422   GDP_BP_REALO(z) = GDP_BPO(z)/PIXGDPO(z);
1423   GDP_BP_W_REALO  = GDP_BP_WO/PIXGDP_WO;
1424   GDP_MP_REALO(z) = GDP_MPO(z)/PIXCONO(z);
1425   IT_REALO(z)     = ITO(z)/PIXINVO(z);
1426   
1427  *==============================================================================
1428  *  4.9 Parameters of the household savings function
1429  *==============================================================================
1430  * sh1O(z)         = [SHO(z)+SGO(z)]/GDP_IBO(z);
1431   sh1O(z)         = [SHO(z)/YDHO(z)];
1432   
1433  * sh0O(z)         = SHO(z)-sh1O(z)*YDHO(z);
1434   sh0O(z) =0 ;
1435  *==============================================================================
1436  *  4.10 Re-calibration of indexed transfers and parameters
1437  *==============================================================================
1438  * sh0O(z)         = sh0O(z)/PIXCONO(z)**eta;
1439   ttdh0O(z)       = ttdh0O(z)/PIXCONO(z)**eta;
1440   
